      "rev_n_12_ae23a1_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_12_ae23a1_0",
        "node_id": "n_12_ae23a1",
        "thought_text": "Analyze the effect of k on the game's outcome. If k = 1, players can indefinitely return to the initial state, leading to a draw. For k > 1, the game's conclusion depends on the initial configuration and the players' strategies.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5255534762166769328",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794411475.358539
      },
      "rev_n_13_121249_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_13_121249_0",
        "node_id": "n_13_121249",
        "thought_text": "Consider the parity of n (number of cards) and k (number of cards flipped in one move). If both n and k are even, Tokitsukaze can always force a win by mirroring Quailty's moves, ensuring the final state is all the same color. If either n or k is odd, the game might end in a draw due to symmetry.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-5985987943321187694",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794412023.5762079
      },
      "rev_n_14_dedd70_0": {
